# build/msc.sh is shipyard's canonical template, carried here VERBATIM: the
# family conventions gate compares it byte for byte with
# $SHIPYARD_SCRIPTS/templates/msc.sh and fails on any difference. So it
# cannot carry a `# shellcheck disable=` line of its own -- adding one here
# would break every product repo's gate at once -- and it cannot be fixed
# locally either. Fix the template in shipyard instead; this file is how we
# lint the rest of build/ without lying about that one.
#
# SC2148: no shebang. It is sourced, never executed; that is the point.
# SC2317: the last line looks unreachable to shellcheck because the line
#         above it can `return`, which only happens when sourced.
# SC2016: the single-quoted CMake snippet it writes must NOT expand here --
#         ${MavericksShipyard_DIR} is for cmake to expand, not the shell.
disable=SC2148,SC2317,SC2016
